#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:1
#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:7
msgid "Uploading data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:3
msgid ""
"This section explains how to upload tabular files, folders with tables "
"and online data to ODE. The tool also ingests other types of format files"
" like PDF, JPEG, etc. However, please note, ODE's main objective is to "
"detect errors on tabular files, the application will **ONLY** show "
"previews for tables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:5
msgid ""
"**Uploading data to ODE is easy\\!** After installing the app and once "
"you open the application on your laptop, you will see this screen:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:7
msgid "![Uploading data](./assets/uploading-data/uploading-data.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:9
msgid ""
"You can click on the **Upload your data** button, located in the centre "
"of the screen or at the top left of the sidebar, to start adding "
"files/folders to the app."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:12
msgid ""
"Each time you upload a file or folder to ODE, the application will not "
"ingest the original file/folder from your computer. Instead, it will make"
" a copy of it and add it to the application folder on your laptop. After "
"the ingestion process ends, you can right-click on the file/folder and "
"select the **Open Location** option. By doing so, ODE will redirect you "
"to the exact location where the copy was saved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:15
msgid "![Open file location](./assets/uploading-data/open-location.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:15
msgid "Open file location"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:17
msgid "Excel, CSV files and folders"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:19
msgid ""
"When clicking on the **Upload your data** button, ODE will display the "
"following dialogue. If you want to upload files or folders, you can do so"
" from the **From Your Computer** section. If you want to add tables that "
"are online, you can do it from **Add External Data**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:21
msgid ""
"![Upload files from your computer](./assets/uploading-data/uploading-"
"data-1.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:21
msgid "Upload files from your computer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:23
msgid ""
"You will see there are two options available in the **From your "
"computer** section. To add file/s, click **Select** on the **Add one or "
"more Excel or csv files** feature. If you want to ingest one or many "
"folders, click Select on the **Add one or more folders** box."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:25
msgid ""
"Once the ingestion process concludes, ODE will add your data to the "
"sidebar of the app:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:27
msgid ""
"![Uploading data sidebar](./assets/uploading-data/uploading-data-"
"sidebar.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:27
msgid "Uploading data sidebar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:29
msgid ""
"Note that while uploading your data, the tool checks your files or "
"folders to find errors according to the validation rules provided by "
"[Frictionless](https://framework.frictionlessdata.io/). Please, check the"
" **Full list of table errors detected** in this guide to learn more."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:31
msgid ""
"Please keep in mind that since the preview section (datagrid) can only "
"show one tabular file at a time, when uploading folders, and after the "
"ingestion process is done, you will need to click on the folder and "
"select the file you want to visualise on the screen. As soon as you click"
" on a specific file, ODE will start validating your data (looking for "
"possible errors), and the table will be shown on the app."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:33
msgid "Tables published online"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:35
msgid ""
"ODE also allows users to upload online tables. You can upload files from "
"open data portals, Google Sheets or tables from your GitHub repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:37
msgid ""
"To upload online tables, first click the **Upload your data** button and "
"then select the **Add External Data** section:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:39
msgid ""
"![Upload online tables](./assets/uploading-data/tables-published-"
"online.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:39
msgid "Upload online tables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:41
msgid "Now, write or paste the URL to the table and click the **Add** button:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:43
msgid ""
"![Upload online table URL input](./assets/uploading-data/tables-"
"published-online-2.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:43
msgid "Upload online table URL input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:45
msgid ""
"After that, ODE will start reviewing your file in the background to "
"detect possible errors, and data will be displayed on the main screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:48
msgid "Before you upload your online table…"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:50
msgid ""
"👉🏼 If you are uploading a Google Sheets file, check that the file is "
"published online. If you don’t know how to do it, please visit [this "
"page](https://support.google.com/docs/answer/183965?hl=en&amp;co=GENIE.Platform%3DDesktop)"
" and follow the steps listed there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:52
msgid ""
"👉🏼 For Google Sheets, please make sure you are adding the public version "
"of your file without the HTML term at the end. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:54
msgid ""
"✅ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1dFVoF6f9VU5pjaGhyyvQaBN0n6ae-"
"iLCtlvsO1N2jhA/edit?gid=0\\#gid=0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:56
msgid ""
"❌ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/e/2PACX-1vQ8w9yb7D-"
"iYEbImb0WD4Kh53\\_Yp7H1VOi1bIMcicphWbkrrH9PobXCJhXt9frqyQ/pubhtml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:58
msgid ""
"👉🏼 When exporting a file from Google Sheets in CSV and you have columns "
"with numbers, please make sure to use “.” for decimals, instead of "
"commas. Otherwise, Frictionless, the code working behind ODE will "
"interpret the content of your cells with numbers as text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:60
msgid "For all tables…"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:62
msgid ""
"👉🏼 Make sure your file is well-organised (well-formatted: each column "
"must contain a name, there should be no extra rows before the table, or "
"additional elements (like borders or lines) next to the space where the "
"tabular data is located."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/uploading-data.md:64
msgid ""
"👉🏼 Check that the tabular data does not contain cells that are merged. "
"Data producers from Governments, international organizations and internal"
" reports usually add tiles, descriptions, and graphs within sheets, like "
"in this case. If there are extra elements in your file, ODE will ingest "
"your file and show you multiple errors."
msgstr ""

